dmission. The original request's real Gitseq-issue dogfood remains open after this correction and must still happen under fresh governance before the implementation can be complete.\n\nDocumentation also needs correction before exact-head approval. docs/concepts/connectors.md changes the outbound and authorization behavior but still rests only on retired inbound artifact 17cb0f7d1f13004e98edf2c110578f31f4f7f7cb. Re-anchor the changed page to the current behavior artifact in accordance with AGENTS.md, then state a fresh exact-head artifact and request review of that new head.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are the Workroom application interpreter/projection and the GitHub connector/CLI surface. Kernel and Nexus behavior are unchanged; the canonical architecture contract is preserved, so architecture.md itself need not change. Security is blocking because ineffective or merely transitively related statements can currently open the inbound authorization door. Simplification: direct-basis membership plus one effective-decision filter is smaller and more precise than the ancestry walk.\n\nExact-head verification passed: go test -count=1 ./cmd/gitseq-github ./internal/connector/github; go vet ./cmd/gitseq-github ./internal/connector/github; git diff --check against the branch merge base.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:be699f9722f641b38b219f1e834a910b8679511d","head":"46ccc0d6321055e898e4a27cb14533d92694a668","verdict":"changes-requested"}}